From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:14:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Dolby Vision: decode both layers and the metadata in the
 FFmpeg decoder

For a stream that takes the native Dolby Vision path
(DVBRIDGE::WantsNativeOutput), CDVDVideoCodecFFmpeg:

- gives FFmpeg the stream's DOVI configuration record, so it exports
  each picture's RPU, and keeps that metadata with the picture;
- decodes a Profile 7 FEL's enhancement layer with dvbridge_fel on a
  second VAAPI decoder (VAAPI.cpp initialises the shared device's
  format table for it) and hands out a base picture only together with
  its enhancement picture. After a seek the demuxer starts from the
  enhancement layer's random-access point (a bounded probe; Kodi keeps
  the requested start time and discards the preroll as usual);
- does not decode a Profile 7 MEL's enhancement layer, which carries no
  residual (decided on the first RPU);
- resynchronises after a pairing fault: the first fault of a title is
  logged with its reason, the pairing restarts (at the next common key
  frame, as after a seek) and base pictures are shown with their
  metadata meanwhile, as for a MEL. After DV_FEL_RESYNCS (3) restarts
  the enhancement layer is not decoded until the next seek. Base
  pictures left without a partner at the end of the stream are shown
  instead of an error. An enhancement decoder that cannot be created
  leaves the title on the base layer and metadata;
- keeps a native stream's last in-band static HDR10 metadata until a
  new SEI replaces it: on streams that carry it only on the first
  IRAP, the next IRAP otherwise read as a format change, the
  renderer was rebuilt and Dolby Vision output restarted (two modesets
  and an HDMI audio reset about one GOP into playback);
- turns a picture's HDR10+ metadata into Profile 8.1 Dolby Vision
  metadata when Convert HDR10+ to Dolby Vision is on, with the engine
  library's optional dvvk_hdr10plus_to_dovi (DVHDR10PlusToDovi.h,
  header dv-engine-vk/dv_engine_vk.h from the yblod-engine-vk package);
- reuses up to four enhancement-layer pictures and shares each frame's
  metadata side-data buffer instead of allocating per picture.

DVDFactoryCodec opens this decoder for native streams and falls through
to the usual decoder chain when it cannot open.

Depends on kodi-9950 (the metadata fields) and kodi-9951 (dvbridge_fel).
Formerly the decoder and demuxer parts of kodi-9990-native-dv,
kodi-9993-fel-presentation-pairing, kodi-9997-dv-static-metadata-latch,
yblod-03, -24 (MEL), -34 (HDR10+), -50 (FEL resync), -51 (decoder
fallback) and -58 (decode allocations).
